  ],
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "> *AI authored to showcase ironpad capabilities.*\n\n# Sorting Visualizer — Interactive Algorithm Comparison\n\n**Sorting** is one of the most fundamental problems in computer science. Comparison-based sorting algorithms — those that determine order purely by comparing elements — have a well-known information-theoretic lower bound:\n\n$$\\Omega(n \\log n)$$\n\nAny algorithm that sorts $n$ elements by comparison alone must make at least $\\log_2(n!)\\approx n\\log_2 n$ comparisons in the worst case.\n\n## Algorithms\n\n| Algorithm      | Average Time   | Worst Time | Space       |\n|----------------|---------------|------------|-------------|\n| **Quicksort**  | $O(n \\log n)$ | $O(n^2)$   | $O(\\log n)$ |\n| **Bubble Sort**| $O(n^2)$      | $O(n^2)$   | $O(1)$      |\n| **Insertion Sort**| $O(n^2)$   | $O(n^2)$   | $O(1)$      |\n\n## Controls\n\nUse the **controls cell** below to adjust the number of elements (20–200) and select which algorithm to visualize. Changing either control restarts the simulation automatically.\n\n## Color Legend\n\n- 🟦 **Steel blue**: unprocessed bars\n- 🟡 **Yellow**: currently being compared\n- 🔴 **Red**: the pivot element (Quicksort only)\n- 🟢 **Green**: confirmed in their final sorted position\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_controls",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Controls",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "(\n    ui::slider(\"num_elements\", 20.0, 200.0)\n        .step(10.0)\n        .label(\"Number of Elements\")\n        .default_value(100.0),\n    ui::dropdown(&[\"Quicksort\", \"Bubble Sort\", \"Insertion Sort\"])\n        .name(\"algorithm\")\n        .label(\"Sorting Algorithm\")\n        .default_value(\"Quicksort\"),\n)",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {},
      "collapsed": true,
      "saved_output": "[{\"Interactive\":{\"kind\":\"slider\",\"config\":\"{\\\"default\\\":100.0,\\\"label\\\":\\\"Number of Elements\\\",\\\"max\\\":200.0,\\\"min\\\":20.0,\\\"name\\\":\\\"num_elements\\\",\\\"step\\\":10.0}\"}},{\"Interactive\":{\"kind\":\"dropdown\",\"config\":\"{\\\"default\\\":\\\"Quicksort\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Sorting Algorithm\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"algorithm\\\",\\\"options\\\":[\\\"Quicksort\\\",\\\"Bubble Sort\\\",\\\"Insertion Sort\\\"]}\"}}]"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Sorting Simulation",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Sorting Visualizer — multiple algorithms with interactive controls.\n//\n// Reads \"num_elements\" (f64) and \"algorithm\" (f64 index) from the sim bus.\n// When either changes, the simulation restarts with the new parameters.\n// Algorithm index: 0 = Quicksort, 1 = Bubble Sort, 2 = Insertion Sort.\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 400;\nconst STEPS_PER_TICK: usize = 4;\n\nfn shuffle(arr: &mut [u32]) {\n    let n = arr.len();\n    let mut seed: u64 = 42;\n    for i in (1..n).rev() {\n        seed = seed.wrapping_mul(6_364_136_223_846_793_005).wrapping_add(1);\n        let j = (seed >> 33) as usize % (i + 1);\n        arr.swap(i, j);\n    }\n}\n\n// ── Algorithm state machines ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n#[derive(Debug)]\nenum QuickPhase {\n    Idle,\n    Partitioning { lo: usize, hi: usize, pivot_val: u32, store: usize, k: usize },\n    Done,\n}\n\nstruct QuickState {\n    stack: Vec<(usize, usize)>,\n    phase: QuickPhase,\n}\n\nimpl QuickState {\n    fn new(n: usize) -> Self {\n        let mut stack = Vec::new();\n        if n > 1 { stack.push((0, n - 1)); }\n        Self { stack, phase: QuickPhase::Idle }\n    }\n\n    fn step(&mut self, arr: &mut [u32], sorted: &mut [bool], stats: &mut (u64, u64)) -> (bool, Option<(usize, usize)>, Option<usize>) {\n        let mut cmp_pair = None;\n        let mut pivot_idx = None;\n        match self.phase {\n            QuickPhase::Done => return (true, None, None),\n            QuickPhase::Idle => {\n                match self.stack.pop() {\n                    None => {\n                        self.phase = QuickPhase::Done;\n                        return (true, None, None);\n                    }\n                    Some((lo, hi)) => {\n                        if lo >= hi {\n                            sorted[lo] = true;\n                        } else {\n                            let pivot_val = arr[hi];\n                            pivot_idx = Some(hi);\n                            self.phase = QuickPhase::Partitioning { lo, hi, pivot_val, store: lo, k: lo };\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            QuickPhase::Partitioning { lo, hi, pivot_val, store, k } => {\n                if k < hi {\n                    stats.0 += 1;\n                    cmp_pair = Some((k, hi));\n                    if arr[k] <= pivot_val {\n                        arr.swap(store, k);\n                        stats.1 += 1;\n                        self.phase = QuickPhase::Partitioning { lo, hi, pivot_val, store: store + 1, k: k + 1 };\n                    } else {\n                        self.phase = QuickPhase::Partitioning { lo, hi, pivot_val, store, k: k + 1 };\n                    }\n                } else {\n                    arr.swap(store, hi);\n                    stats.1 += 1;\n                    sorted[store] = true;\n                    if store > lo {\n                        self.stack.push((lo, store - 1));\n                    } else {\n                        sorted[lo] = true;\n                    }\n                    if store + 1 <= hi {\n                        self.stack.push((store + 1, hi));\n                    } else {\n                        sorted[hi] = true;\n                    }\n                    self.phase = QuickPhase::Idle;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        (false, cmp_pair, pivot_idx)\n    }\n}\n\nstruct BubbleState {\n    i: usize,\n    j: usize,\n    n: usize,\n    done: bool,\n}\n\nimpl BubbleState {\n    fn new(n: usize) -> Self {\n        Self { i: 0, j: 0, n, done: n <= 1 }\n    }\n\n    fn step(&mut self, arr: &mut [u32], sorted: &mut [bool], stats: &mut (u64, u64)) -> (bool, Option<(usize, usize)>, Option<usize>) {\n        if self.done { return (true, None, None); }\n        let bound = self.n - 1 - self.i;\n        if self.j >= bound {\n            sorted[bound] = true;\n            self.i += 1;\n            self.j = 0;\n            if self.i >= self.n - 1 {\n                self.done = true;\n                if self.n > 0 { sorted[0] = true; }\n                return (true, None, None);\n            }\n            return (false, None, None);\n        }\n        stats.0 += 1;\n        let cmp = Some((self.j, self.j + 1));\n        if arr[self.j] > arr[self.j + 1] {\n            arr.swap(self.j, self.j + 1);\n            stats.1 += 1;\n        }\n        self.j += 1;\n        (false, cmp, None)\n    }\n}\n\nstruct InsertionState {\n    i: usize,\n    j: usize,\n    n: usize,\n    inserting: bool,\n    done: bool,\n}\n\nimpl InsertionState {\n    fn new(n: usize) -> Self {\n        let mut s = Self { i: 1, j: 0, n, inserting: false, done: n <= 1 };\n        if n > 0 { /* element 0 is trivially sorted */ }\n        s\n    }\n\n    fn step(&mut self, arr: &mut [u32], sorted: &mut [bool], stats: &mut (u64, u64)) -> (bool, Option<(usize, usize)>, Option<usize>) {\n        if self.done { return (true, None, None); }\n        if !self.inserting {\n            if self.i >= self.n {\n                self.done = true;\n                return (true, None, None);\n            }\n            self.j = self.i;\n            self.inserting = true;\n        }\n        if self.j > 0 {\n            stats.0 += 1;\n            let cmp = Some((self.j - 1, self.j));\n            if arr[self.j - 1] > arr[self.j] {\n                arr.swap(self.j - 1, self.j);\n                stats.1 += 1;\n                self.j -= 1;\n                return (false, cmp, Some(self.j));\n            }\n        }\n        sorted[self.i] = true;\n        self.i += 1;\n        self.inserting = false;\n        (false, None, None)\n    }\n}\n\nenum AlgoState {\n    Quick(QuickState),\n    Bubble(BubbleState),\n    Insertion(InsertionState),\n}\n\nimpl AlgoState {\n    fn step(&mut self, arr: &mut [u32], sorted: &mut [bool], stats: &mut (u64, u64)) -> (bool, Option<(usize, usize)>, Option<usize>) {\n        match self {\n            Self::Quick(s) => s.step(arr, sorted, stats),\n            Self::Bubble(s) => s.step(arr, sorted, stats),\n            Self::Insertion(s) => s.step(arr, sorted, stats),\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// ── Simulation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nstruct SortVis {\n    arr: Vec<u32>,\n    algo: AlgoState,\n    comparisons: u64,\n    swaps: u64,\n    sorted_done: bool,\n    comparing: Option<(usize, usize)>,\n    pivot_highlight: Option<usize>,\n    sorted_indices: Vec<bool>,\n    sweep: usize,\n    prev_n: usize,\n    prev_algo: u32,\n}\n\nimpl SortVis {\n    fn reset(&mut self, n: usize, algo_idx: u32) {\n        let n = n.clamp(2, 200);\n        self.arr = (1..=n as u32).collect();\n        shuffle(&mut self.arr);\n        self.algo = match algo_idx {\n            1 => AlgoState::Bubble(BubbleState::new(n)),\n            2 => AlgoState::Insertion(InsertionState::new(n)),\n            _ => AlgoState::Quick(QuickState::new(n)),\n        };\n        self.comparisons = 0;\n        self.swaps = 0;\n        self.sorted_done = false;\n        self.comparing = None;\n        self.pivot_highlight = None;\n        self.sorted_indices = vec![false; n];\n        self.sweep = 0;\n        self.prev_n = n;\n        self.prev_algo = algo_idx;\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Simulation for SortVis {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        let n = 100;\n        let mut arr: Vec<u32> = (1..=n as u32).collect();\n        shuffle(&mut arr);\n        Self {\n            arr,\n            algo: AlgoState::Quick(QuickState::new(n)),\n            comparisons: 0,\n            swaps: 0,\n            sorted_done: false,\n            comparing: None,\n            pivot_highlight: None,\n            sorted_indices: vec![false; n],\n            sweep: 0,\n            prev_n: n,\n            prev_algo: 0,\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> Canvas {\n        let cur_n = sim::read::<f64>(\"num_elements\").unwrap_or(100.0) as usize;\n        let cur_algo = sim::read::<f64>(\"algorithm\").unwrap_or(0.0) as u32;\n\n        if cur_n != self.prev_n || cur_algo != self.prev_algo {\n            self.reset(cur_n, cur_algo);\n        }\n\n        let n = self.arr.len();\n\n        for _ in 0..STEPS_PER_TICK {\n            if self.sorted_done { break; }\n            let mut stats = (self.comparisons, self.swaps);\n            let (done, cmp, piv) = self.algo.step(&mut self.arr, &mut self.sorted_indices, &mut stats);\n            self.comparisons = stats.0;\n            self.swaps = stats.1;\n            self.comparing = cmp;\n            if piv.is_some() { self.pivot_highlight = piv; }\n            if done {\n                self.sorted_done = true;\n                self.comparing = None;\n                self.pivot_highlight = None;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if self.sorted_done && self.sweep < n {\n            let end = (self.sweep + 5).min(n);\n            for i in self.sweep..end {\n                self.sorted_indices[i] = true;\n            }\n            self.sweep = end;\n        }\n\n        let algo_name = match cur_algo { 1 => \"Bubble Sort\", 2 => \"Insertion Sort\", _ => \"Quicksort\" };\n        sim::emit(\"comparisons\", &self.comparisons);\n        sim::emit(\"swaps\", &self.swaps);\n        sim::emit(\"sorted\", &self.sorted_done);\n        sim::emit(\"algo_name\", &algo_name);\n        sim::emit(\"num_elements_val\", &(n as u64));\n\n        // ── Render ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n        let bar_w_f = W as f64 / n as f64;\n        let mut canvas = Canvas::new(W, H);\n        canvas.fill((26, 26, 46));\n\n        let comparing_pair = self.comparing;\n        let pivot_idx = self.pivot_highlight;\n\n        for i in 0..n {\n            let val = self.arr[i];\n            let bar_h = (val as u32 * (H - 4)) / n as u32;\n            let x0 = (i as f64 * bar_w_f) as u32;\n            let x1 = ((i + 1) as f64 * bar_w_f) as u32;\n            let y0 = H - bar_h;\n\n            let color = if self.sorted_indices[i] {\n                (68, 204, 68)\n            } else if Some(i) == pivot_idx {\n                (255, 68, 68)\n            } else if comparing_pair.map_or(false, |(a, b)| i == a || i == b) {\n                (255, 215, 0)\n            } else {\n                (70, 130, 180)\n            };\n\n            let gap = if x1 > x0 + 1 { 1 } else { 0 };\n            for x in x0..x1.saturating_sub(gap) {\n                for y in y0..H {\n                    canvas.set_pixel(x, y, color);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        canvas\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        30\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {},
      "collapsed": true,
      "saved_output": "[{\"Text\":\"(output too large to embed; run the cell to regenerate it)\"}]"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2",
      "order": 3,
      "label": "Statistics",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "struct Stats {\n    tick: u32,\n}\n\nimpl LiveView for Stats {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        Self { tick: 0 }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> LiveContent {\n        self.tick += 1;\n        let comps = sim::read::<u64>(\"comparisons\").unwrap_or(0);\n        let swaps = sim::read::<u64>(\"swaps\").unwrap_or(0);\n        let done = sim::read::<bool>(\"sorted\").unwrap_or(false);\n        let algo = sim::read::<String>(\"algo_name\").unwrap_or_else(|| \"Quicksort\".into());\n        let n = sim::read::<u64>(\"num_elements_val\").unwrap_or(100);\n\n        let status = if done { \"✅ SORTED\" } else { \"⏳ SORTING...\" };\n        let color = if done { \"#44cc44\" } else { \"#ffd700\" };\n\n        LiveContent::Html(format!(r##\"<div style=\"font-family: monospace; background: #1a1a2e; color: #e0e0e0; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; display: flex; gap: 32px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n            <div><span style=\"color: #888;\">Algorithm:</span> <span style=\"color: #bb86fc; font-size: 1.3em;\">{algo}</span></div>\n            <div><span style=\"color: #888;\">Elements:</span> <span style=\"color: #80cbc4; font-size: 1.3em;\">{n}</span></div>\n            <div><span style=\"color: #888;\">Comparisons:</span> <span style=\"color: #4fc3f7; font-size: 1.3em;\">{comps}</span></div>\n            <div><span style=\"color: #888;\">Swaps:</span> <span style=\"color: #ff6b6b; font-size: 1.3em;\">{swaps}</span></div>\n            <div><span style=\"color: {color}; font-size: 1.3em; font-weight: bold;\">{status}</span></div>\n        </div>\"##))\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        5\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {},
      "collapsed": true,
      "saved_output": "[{\"LiveView\":{\"fps\":5,\"kind\":\"html\",\"content\":\"<div style=\\\"font-family: monospace; background: #1a1a2e; color: #e0e0e0; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; display: flex; gap: 32px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;\\\">\\n            <div><span style=\\\"color: #888;\\\">Algorithm:</span> <span style=\\\"color: #bb86fc; font-size: 1.3em;\\\">Quicksort</span></div>\\n            <div><span style=\\\"color: #888;\\\">Elements:</span> <span style=\\\"color: #80cbc4; font-size: 1.3em;\\\">100</span></div>\\n            <div><span style=\\\"color: #888;\\\">Comparisons:</span> <span style=\\\"color: #4fc3f7; font-size: 1.3em;\\\">55</span></div>\\n            <div><span style=\\\"color: #888;\\\">Swaps:</span> <span style=\\\"color: #ff6b6b; font-size: 1.3em;\\\">18</span></div>\\n            <div><span style=\\\"color: #ffd700; font-size: 1.3em; font-weight: bold;\\\">⏳ SORTING...</span></div>\\n        </div>\"}}]"
    }
  ]
}
